<section class="example-section">
  {{#> important-callout}}
  This guide can be used in general to sign bitcoin core transactions between an online node and an offline node.
  {{/important-callout}}

  <p>Make sure to follow the <a href="../setup-devices/requirements.hbs" target="_blank">guide</a> to setup online and offline devices before you continue with this guide.</p>

  <h2>Sign transactions</h2>
  <p>The process is as follows:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Input encrypted backup to obtain binary</li>
    <li>Input one-time pad to decrypt backup into a seedphrase</li>
    <li>Input passphrase to derive BIP39 wallet</li>
    <li>Run python script for bitcoin core private descriptors off BIP39</li>
    <li>Import private descriptors into bitcoin core</li>
    <li>Derive public descriptor and transfer it to online device</li>
    <li>Online device creates PSBT and transfer it to offline device</li>
    <li>Offline device signs PSBT and transfers it to online device</li>
    <li>Online device verifies and broadcasts signed transaction</li>
  </ul>

